<title>FRANCE: French industrial production down 0.6 pct in March.</title>
<headline>French industrial production down 0.6 pct in March.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE said on Thursday industrial production, excluding construction, fell 0.6 percent in March from the previous month and was up 1.2 percent percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Industrial production excluding energy, agri-food businesses and construction -- considered by INSEE the best measure of manufacturing output -- rose 0.4 percent percent in March from the previous month, giving a year-on-year rise of 2.3 percent.  </p>
<p>INSEE gave the following seasonally adjusted percentage changes:</p>
<p>					Mar vs Feb  Feb vs Jan   yr/yr</p>
<p> Industrial production index     -0.6	  1.7	   1.2</p>
<p> Manufacturing output		 0.4	  3.9	   2.3</p>
<p> Agri-food			     -1.9	  2.2	   2.6</p>
<p> Consumer goods			 0.9	  0.2	  -0.3</p>
<p> Car industry			  -0.9	  5.1	   0.7</p>
<p> Industrial capital goods	   0.7	  2.2	   1.3</p>
<p> Semi-finished goods		  0.4	  5.8	   4.1</p>
<p> Energy				  -5.5	 -9.4	  -5.8</p>
<p> Construction			   0.9	 13.5	   0.1</p>
<p>Comparison with year ago period is for three months to end March versus the same period in the three months in the same period last year.</p>
<p>It also gave the following seasonally adjusted data based on a new index introduced in January 1996.</p>
<p>						     Mar 97 Feb 97  Mar 96</p>
<p> Industrial production index (base 1990) 100.5  101.1   99.4</p>
<p> Manufacturing output			   98.7   98.3   95.4</p>
<p>   Agri-food				     110.5  112.6  108.0</p>
<p>   Consumer goods				 97.5   96.6   97.5</p>
<p>   Car Industry				  104.9  105.9  104.0</p>
<p>   Industrial capital goods		   87.4   86.8   85.2</p>
<p>   Semi-finished goods			 104.7  104.3   99.0</p>
<p>   Energy					  104.0  110.0  118.2</p>
<p>   Construction				   93.1   92.3   91.2</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
